DoD 3 / DoD 4 EVIDENCE — FOUR PROCESS-LOCAL MUTATION DRILLS (worker-a11dcf70, 2026-09-09)

NOTHING WAS WRITTEN TO THE REPOSITORY. Every mutant lived only inside a Vite pre-transform in a throwaway config outside the tree, the technique task-4a9d95cf proved on this same file. No gate lease was needed, no peer run could collide, and there is no restore proof to get wrong because no repo byte was ever mutated. Proof below, and the config's FULL SOURCE is inline at the end so a grader can recreate and re-run it.

Invocation, identical for every row:
  MOE_REPO_ROOT=D:/projexts/moe-next MOE_DRILL_MUTATION=<name> pnpm exec vitest run --config "%TEMP%/moe-task-39e1628f68f54b8694bfd4a9a8a1b0ad-worker-a11dcf70-drill.config.mjs" --reporter=verbose

CONTROL — the harness itself is green and executes all twelve arms:
  exit 0 · `Test Files  1 passed (1)` · `Tests  12 passed (12)` · this arm 307ms
Without this row the drills below would prove nothing: a harness that runs no tests fails every mutation for free.

DRILL (i) — THE BUDGET IS LOAD-BEARING. mutation `budget-200` rewrites ONLY the SECOND `}, 30_000);` (mine, :218) to `}, 200);`, well under the 242-277ms measured range. The transform asserts there are exactly two occurrences and that the arm's `it(` opener sits BETWEEN them, so it cannot silently hit the sibling's :194.
  exit 1 · `Test Files  1 failed (1)` · `Tests  1 failed | 11 passed (12)`
  FAIL … > never lets a caller-supplied SHA stand in for observed Git authority
  Error: Test timed out in 200ms.
  ❯ packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-pinned-documents.test.ts:200:3
A TIMEOUT naming the reduced number, on this arm alone, with the other ELEVEN still passing. A budget nothing can fail against is not evidence; this one fails.
(Worth recording because it is not obvious: the arm's body is fully SYNCHRONOUS — `execFileSync` throughout — so one might expect vitest to be unable to abort it. Vitest 4.1.10 still reds it on elapsed time after the body returns. Measured, not assumed.)

DRILL (ii) — THE BUDGET DID NOT MAKE A BROKEN ARM GREEN. Three separate PRODUCTION mutations in packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-pinned-documents.ts, because the two conditions DoD 3 names take different paths: UNSET refuses in `resolveCorpusRoot` (:96) before any git spawn, DIRTY refuses in `observePinnedCorpusAuthority` (:151) only after `observeCorpusGit` returns. One mutation cannot reach both.

  (ii-a) `unset-code` — :96 `preFreezeAuditRefusal("CORPUS_ROOT_UNSET", 0, "")` becomes `…("CORPUS_ROOT_UNVERSIONED", 0, "")`.
    exit 1 · `Tests  5 failed | 7 passed (12)`
    AssertionError: expected 'CORPUS_ROOT_UNVERSIONED' to be 'CORPUS_ROOT_UNSET' // Object.is equality
    ❯ packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-pinned-documents.test.ts:206:65
    Red ON THE ASSERTION at :206, the CORPUS_ROOT_UNSET clause. Not a timeout.

  (ii-b) `dirty-code` — :151 `if (observed.status.length > 0) return preFreezeAuditRefusal("CORPUS_ROOT_DIRTY", 0, root);` becomes the same call with `"CORPUS_ROOT_UNVERSIONED"`.
    exit 1 · `Tests  2 failed | 10 passed (12)`
    AssertionError: expected 'CORPUS_ROOT_UNVERSIONED' to be 'CORPUS_ROOT_DIRTY' // Object.is equality
    ❯ packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-pinned-documents.test.ts:209:65
    Red ON THE ASSERTION at :209, the CORPUS_ROOT_DIRTY clause. Not a timeout.

  (ii-c) `dirty-layer` — the same :151 line becomes a frozen literal keeping the CODE correct and carrying `layer: "NOT_PRE_FREEZE_AUDIT"`, so the red must land on the LAYER clause rather than the code one.
    exit 1 · `Tests  2 failed | 10 passed (12)`
    AssertionError: expected 'NOT_PRE_FREEZE_AUDIT' to be 'PRE_FREEZE_AUDIT' // Object.is equality
    ❯ packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-pinned-documents.test.ts:210:66
    Red ON THE ASSERTION at :210, the PRE_FREEZE_AUDIT layer clause. Not a timeout.
    NOTE ON WHY IT IS SHAPED THAT WAY: mutating `PRE_FREEZE_AUDIT_LAYER` at pre-freeze-audit-vocabulary.ts:71 would be VACUOUS — the test imports that same constant, so expectation and production would move together and the arm would stay green. The mutation therefore breaks the value the factory emits at one call site, leaving the test's expectation anchored.

So all three DoD 3 conditions red on an assertion naming the exact expected code or layer, and only drill (i) reds on a timeout. That contrast is the point: the 30s budget bounds the arm without weakening any of its refusal assertions.

DoD 4 — THE OTHER ELEVEN ARMS ARE UNCHANGED.
  $ grep -n "^  }, " packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-pinned-documents.test.ts
  194:  }, 30_000);      <- the sibling moved-tree arm's, landed by task-4a9d95cf, untouched
  218:  }, 30_000);      <- mine
  Exactly TWO lines, against exactly ONE before this row (recorded in the step-1 note).
  $ git diff --stat -- packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-pinned-documents.test.ts
   packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-pinned-documents.test.ts | 9 ++++++++-
   1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
  $ git diff -U0 … | grep "^@@"
  @@ -211 +211,8 @@
  A SINGLE hunk, at :211, inside the one `it` (:200-218). Nothing outside it moved.

TREE IS BYTE-IDENTICAL WHERE IT SHOULD BE, AFTER ALL FOUR DRILLS:
  $ git status --porcelain -- <test file> <prod file> <vocabulary file>
   M packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-pinned-documents.test.ts
  (the production module and the vocabulary module do not appear at all)
  $ git diff --stat -- pre-freeze-pinned-documents.ts pre-freeze-audit-vocabulary.ts
  (empty — and these are TRACKED files, so an empty diff is a valid proof for them; the untracked-path hazard does not apply)
  $ grep -rn 'NOT_PRE_FREEZE_AUDIT|CORPUS_ROOT_MUTANT|}, 200);' packages/benchmark/src/
  NONE
No mutant token survives anywhere under packages/benchmark/src.

FULL SOURCE OF THE DRILL CONFIG (written to %TEMP%/moe-task-39e1628f68f54b8694bfd4a9a8a1b0ad-worker-a11dcf70-drill.config.mjs, deleted after the drills; recreate verbatim to re-run):

const TEST_TARGET = "pre-freeze-pinned-documents.test.ts";
const PROD_TARGET = "pre-freeze-pinned-documents.ts";
const mutation = process.env.MOE_DRILL_MUTATION ?? "";
const BUDGET_ANCHOR = "[newline]  }, 30_000);";                 // literal newline, then two spaces
const UNSET_ANCHOR = 'preFreezeAuditRefusal("CORPUS_ROOT_UNSET", 0, "")';
const DIRTY_ANCHOR = 'if (observed.status.length > 0) return preFreezeAuditRefusal("CORPUS_ROOT_DIRTY", 0, root);';
const replaceOnly = (code, anchor, replacement, label) => {
  const first = code.indexOf(anchor);
  if (first < 0) throw new Error("DRILL_ANCHOR_MISSING " + label);
  if (code.indexOf(anchor, first + 1) >= 0) throw new Error("DRILL_ANCHOR_AMBIGUOUS " + label);
  return code.slice(0, first) + replacement + code.slice(first + anchor.length);
};
const mutateTest = (code) => {
  if (mutation !== "budget-200") return code;
  const first = code.indexOf(BUDGET_ANCHOR);
  const second = code.indexOf(BUDGET_ANCHOR, first + 1);
  const third = second < 0 ? -1 : code.indexOf(BUDGET_ANCHOR, second + 1);
  if (first < 0 || second < 0) throw new Error("DRILL_ANCHOR_MISSING budget (need two)");
  if (third >= 0) throw new Error("DRILL_ANCHOR_AMBIGUOUS budget (found three)");
  const armAt = code.indexOf('it("never lets a caller-supplied SHA stand in for observed Git authority"');
  if (armAt < 0) throw new Error("DRILL_ARM_MISSING");
  if (!(first < armAt && armAt < second)) throw new Error("DRILL_ANCHOR_WRONG_OCCURRENCE");
  return code.slice(0, second) + "[newline]  }, 200);" + code.slice(second + BUDGET_ANCHOR.length);
};
const mutateProd = (code) => {
  if (mutation === "unset-code") return replaceOnly(code, UNSET_ANCHOR, 'preFreezeAuditRefusal("CORPUS_ROOT_UNVERSIONED", 0, "")', "unset-code");
  if (mutation === "dirty-code") return replaceOnly(code, DIRTY_ANCHOR, 'if (observed.status.length > 0) return preFreezeAuditRefusal("CORPUS_ROOT_UNVERSIONED", 0, root);', "dirty-code");
  if (mutation === "dirty-layer") return replaceOnly(code, DIRTY_ANCHOR, 'if (observed.status.length > 0) return Object.freeze({ code: "CORPUS_ROOT_DIRTY", layer: "NOT_PRE_FREEZE_AUDIT", line: 0, ok: false, token: root });', "dirty-layer");
  return code;
};
const KNOWN = ["", "budget-200", "unset-code", "dirty-code", "dirty-layer"];
if (!KNOWN.includes(mutation)) throw new Error("DRILL_UNKNOWN_MUTATION " + mutation);
export default {
  root: process.env.MOE_REPO_ROOT,
  plugins: [{ name: "moe-drill", enforce: "pre",
    transform(code, id) {
      if (id.endsWith(TEST_TARGET)) return mutateTest(code);
      if (id.endsWith(PROD_TARGET)) return mutateProd(code);
      return null;
    } }],
  test: { environment: "node", include: ["packages/benchmark/src/pre-freeze-pinned-documents.test.ts"], pool: "forks", isolate: true, passWithNoTests: false },
};

Two notes for whoever reuses it. `[newline]` above stands for a real newline escape in the source, spelled out here because a literal backslash-n in a comment is ambiguous. Do NOT import `defineConfig` from "vitest/config" in a config outside the repo — it cannot resolve node_modules and dies with `Cannot find package 'vitest'`; a plain object export is what works. `PROD_TARGET` cannot collide with `TEST_TARGET` because "…documents.test.ts" does not end with "…documents.ts".
